// EXPECT: [E086]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 11, Col 5: arithmetic is not provably free of overflow
// A character literal is a u8, 0..255. One at or above 0x80 (`\xHH`, the only spelling that makes
// one) was stored in a signed `char`, so `'\xff'` reached the IR as the constant -1. The range
// analysis then proved `c + 1` fits a u8 (it computed 0), the obligation was discharged, and the
// program returned 0: a silent wrap of 255 + 1. The same program with `c u8 = 255` was refused.
// The C ran "right" in plain use (its slot is uint8_t) and the interpreter shared the wrong
// constant, so no oracle saw it.
func main() i32 {
    c = '\xff'
    d u8 = c + 1
    return d as i32
}
